1
00:04:23,478 --> 00:04:29,478
If you could be God for one week, what would you do?

2
00:08:46,956 --> 00:08:52,956
Bruce Almighty is a fantasy, comedy film directed by Tom Shadyac.

3
00:13:10,434 --> 00:13:16,434
Bruce Nolan toils as a "human interest" television reporter in Buffalo, NY, but despite his
high ratings and the love of his beautiful girlfriend, Bruce remains unfulfilled.

4
00:17:33,913 --> 00:17:39,913
At the end of the worst day in his life, he angrily ridicules God — and the
Almighty responds, endowing Bruce with all of His divine powers.

5
00:21:57,391 --> 00:22:03,391
Bruce Nolan, played by Jim Carrey.

6
00:26:20,869 --> 00:26:26,869
God, played by Morgan Freeman.

7
00:30:44,347 --> 00:30:50,347
Grace Connelly, played by Jennifer Aniston.

8
00:35:07,826 --> 00:35:13,826
Jack Baylor, played by Philip Baker Hall.

9
00:39:31,304 --> 00:39:37,304
Susan Ortega, played by Catherine Bell.

10
00:43:54,782 --> 00:44:00,782
Debbie, played by Lisa Ann Walter.

11
00:48:18,260 --> 00:48:24,260
Bruce Almighty is a 2003 American fantasy comedy film starring Jim Carrey.

12
00:52:41,739 --> 00:52:47,739
The film follows Bruce Nolan, a down-on-his-luck television reporter who complains to God (played by Morgan Freeman)
that he is not doing his job correctly and is offered the chance to try being God himself for one week.

13
00:57:05,217 --> 00:57:11,217
The film was directed by Tom Shadyac and written by Steve
Koren, Mark O'Keefe and Steve Oedekerk.

14
01:01:28,695 --> 01:01:34,695
Jennifer Aniston, Steve Carell, Philip Baker Hall and Catherine Bell also star.

15
01:05:52,173 --> 01:05:58,173
The film is Shadyac and Carrey's third collaboration, after Ace
Ventura: Pet Detective (1994) and Liar Liar (1997).

16
01:10:15,652 --> 01:10:21,652
When released in American theaters on May 23, 2003 by Universal Pictures, Bruce Almighty received mixed reviews from critics but
was a box-office success and grossed $86.4 million in its opening weekend, a Memorial Day record at the time.

17
01:14:39,130 --> 01:14:45,130
The film surprised the industry's pundits when it beat
The Matrix Reloaded the following weekend.

18
01:19:02,608 --> 01:19:08,608
It went on to gross $484 million worldwide, becoming the fifth-highest-grossing
film of 2003 and Universal 4th highest grossing film when released.

19
01:23:26,086 --> 01:23:32,086
Evan Almighty — a spin-off sequel focusing on Steve Carell's character, with Shadyac and Oedekerk returning to
direct and write, respectively, and Freeman also reprising his role — was released on June 22, 2007.

20
01:27:49,565 --> 01:27:55,565
In addition, three Indian remakes of the film - Krishnarjuna (Telugu-speaking), Arai En 305-il
Kadavul (Tamil-speaking), and God Tussi Great Ho (Hindi-speaking) - were released in 2008.

21
01:32:13,043 --> 01:32:19,043
The film explores themes of new love, lovesickness, moon, street gang, moses.

22
01:36:36,521 --> 01:36:42,521
The tone is lighthearted.
